# Progress

A horizontal bar showing how much of a measurable operation is
complete. Basecoat ships no component — a track holding a fill, built
from utilities, with `role="progressbar"` and aria kept in sync with
the width.

<%= embed :progress, :default %>

```html
<div class="bg-primary/20 relative h-2 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-full"
     role="progressbar" aria-label="Importing referrals"
     aria-valuenow="60" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100">
  <div class="bg-primary h-full transition-all" style="width: 60%"></div>
</div>
```

## When to use

- Multi-step operations with a real completion fraction: imports,
  uploads, multi-stage processing.
- Showing completeness of a thing, not just a wait — e.g. profile or
  form completion.

## When not to use

- Unknown duration or progress — use `spinner`. A bar that crawls
  and stalls is worse than no bar (see the *Feedback* pattern page).
- Loading page content — use `skeleton`.

## Anatomy and options

Two nested elements: a track (`bg-primary/20 relative h-2 w-full
overflow-hidden rounded-full`) holding a fill (`bg-primary h-full
transition-all`) whose `width` carries the percentage. `transition-all`
animates value changes, so stepwise updates read as movement without
any JS. Clamp the percentage to 0–100 before writing it.

## Do and don't

- Do drive `width` and `aria-valuenow` from real units of work
  (records processed, bytes sent) — never from elapsed time.
- Do pair the bar with a visible count when one exists ("32 of 120
  records") rather than relying on the bar alone.
- Don't park the bar at a high value while waiting on a final step;
  if the last step's duration is unknown, the operation wants a
  spinner for that phase.
- Don't use a progress bar as a static gauge of unrelated quantities
  (capacity, score) — it signals an operation in progress.

## Accessibility and content

- `role="progressbar"` with `aria-valuenow` / `-valuemin` /
  `-valuemax` kept in sync with the fill width — screen readers get
  the same number sighted users see.
- `aria-label` names the operation: "Importing referrals".
